  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <div class="section-heading">Conclusions</div>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Our data set lags other a few updates window into licensed and unlicensed cannabis flower retail prices in California. We find that the licensing premium is substantial, with licensed cannabis flower averaging <span data-field="conclusion_price_summary">{{ conclusion_price_summary }}</span> per gram, while unlicensed flower averages <span data-field="conclusion_price_summary_2">{{ conclusion_price_summary_2 }}</span> per gram. This difference, which we call a "licensing premium," conceals more complex relationships between the sample source. Store retailers operate storefronts while far more operate delivery-only services. Figure 1 compares flower averages prices at delivery-only retailers and storefront retailers. The average licens-ing premium is about <span data-field="conclusion_premium_summary">{{ conclusion_premium_summary }}</span> times higher at storefronts (<span data-field="conclusion_storefront_premium_percentage">{{ conclusion_storefront_premium_percentage }}</span>) than at delivery-only prices (<span data-field="conclusion_delivery_premium_percentage">{{ conclusion_delivery_premium_percentage }}</span>). In the unlicensed market, storefronts are <span data-field="conclusion_storefront_unlicensed_premium">{{ conclusion_storefront_unlicensed_premium }}</span> higher.</p>
